# AMI Meeting Corpus (Mix-Headset condition) -- per-file SHA-256 manifest
# Source corpus release: AMI public corpus, all 171 available Mix-Headset WAVs
#   selected 2026-08-02; manual annotations v1.6.2; automatic annotations v1.5.1
#   (scripts/data/datasets.lock.json, dataset "ami-meeting-corpus").
# Generated: 2026-08-20, by direct `sha256sum` over the local corpus under
#   $SPEECHRL_DATA_DIR/datasets/ami (WSL2 Ubuntu-24.04, primary dev machine), one
#   read pass, no parallelism.
# Paths below are relative to the AMI root ($SPEECHRL_DATA_DIR/datasets/ami), i.e.
#   the same root scripts/data/datasets.lock.json's "ami-meeting-corpus" entry uses
#   for its expected_layout.
# Aggregate-closure provenance this manifest supersedes for the per-file case: the
#   umbrella lock's own hash_coverage_note for this dataset (see
#   scripts/data/datasets.lock.json) records only a per-archive SHA-256 for the two
#   annotation zips plus an aggregate payload_manifest_sha256 over all 174 payload
#   files -- not a per-WAV hash -- so scripts/data/verify.py falls back to
#   file-count + total-size closure for the audio tree. This file closes that
#   per-file gap by direct computation on the primary dev machine; it does not
#   change, and was not cross-checked against, any umbrella-private per-file hash
#   (none exists for the individual WAVs).
# Verify: cd "$SPEECHRL_DATA_DIR/datasets/ami" && sha256sum -c docs/ami-file-manifest.sha256
#   (run from this repository's root with a path adjustment, or copy this file next
#   to the AMI root first).
